, tornadoes, floods, mudslides, wildfires or other natural disasters; (vi) the public announcement or pendency of this Agreement; (vii) any action taken or refrained from being taken, in each case to which Parent has expressly approved; (viii) changes or proposed changes in GAAP or other accounting standards or Law; (ix) changes in the price or trading volume of the Company Common Stock or Indebtedness of the Company and its Subsidiaries; (x) any failure, in and of itself, by the Company and its Subsidiaries to meet any public estimates or expectations of the Company\u2019s revenue, earnings or other financial performance or results of operations for any period; and (xi) Transaction Litigation; provided further, that with respect to clauses (i) through (v) and (viii) of this definition, such Effects shall be taken into account in determining whether a \u201cCompany Material Adverse Effect\u201d has occurred or would reasonably be expected to occur, in each case, to the extent that such Effect has had a disproportionate adverse effect on the Company and its Subsidiaries relative to other companies operating in the industries in which the Company and its Subsidiaries conduct business. (Pages 12-13)\nAnswer:
